      "metadataURI" : "CIMPATH=Metadata/d6f1f129fa850a04f65cc7417a7dd982.xml",
      "useSourceMetadata" : false,
      "description" : "The Building Feature Class provides descriptive and location information about existing Forest Service owned buildings and existing non-FS owned buildings that are located on Forest Service lands. The descriptive information includes: The type and current use of buildings and the planned future use, the buildings containing a system (electrical, mechanical, plumbing), the replacement cost of the building in current dollars, the facility condition rating describing the building's condition. The location information includes: The region, forest, and district on which the building sits, the type of Forest Service land unit on which it resides (e.g. recreation site, administrative site, etc), the latitude/longitude, the state, county, and congressional district. This is a published feature class and is constructed by reformatting data stored in the Infra database and managed by the individual administrative units. This feature class is not used for data entry or editing.",
